{
  "README": [
    "The negative corpus for contract.jq, consumed by self-test-validate.sh.",
    "",
    "Each case is ONE targeted mutation of a known-good generated definition, so",
    "the diagnostic it provokes is attributable: the base file is asserted clean",
    "in the same run, therefore any code the mutant reports was caused by the",
    "mutation. That is why these are derived rather than authored as standalone",
    "broken files \u2014 a hand-written broken file proves the validator rejected",
    "something, not that it rejected the thing you meant.",
    "",
    "Fields: `code` is the diagnostic the case must provoke. `name` identifies it.",
    "Either `base` + `mutate` (a jq expression applied to that generated",
    "definition) or `raw` (literal file bytes, for cases that must not be valid",
    "JSON). `severity` defaults to \"error\"; \"warn\" cases must NOT fail plain",
    "validation and MUST fail --strict. `trap` tags the four authoring traps",
    "called out in contract.jq, and self-test-validate.sh asserts all four are",
    "represented.",
    "",
    "Sorted by (code, name). self-test-validate.sh enforces both that ordering and",
    "that every code contract.jq and validate-workflow.sh can emit appears here."
  ],
